{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The 5.00 SGD in issue is not on the rider today. The payments ledger records payment_status REFUNDED with refund_issued_sgd 5.00 after the rider's complaint, and the filing party is the DRIVER, so the only way the rider ends up carrying the disputed charge is a ruling that moves it back onto him. Under POL-GEN-03 a ruling of NO_ACTION preserves the present state and 'never means restore a charge'. The rider's case is therefore put on this trip's own evidence and on the clause that governs it, not on the platform's no-show automation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-21 gives the rider of a scheduled trip whose driver arrives early the full free wait measured from the scheduled pickup time, so the protected window on this booking ran from 07:45:00 to 07:50:00 - exactly what the trip record's own derived free_wait block states (starts_from scheduled_at, starts_at 07:45:00, ends_at 07:50:00, free_wait_sec 300). The platform's wait timer on this trip nevertheless started at 07:39:35, on the driver's early arrival, and expired at 07:44:35 - before the rider's booked pickup time. The no-show here was therefore processed on a start POL-NS-21 does not authorise, and the 'wait_timer_expired' event at 07:44:35 cannot itself carry the charge. The rider states plainly that the derivation puts the corrected deadline at 07:50:00 and that the 07:51:40 cancellation falls after it; his point is that the 5.00 was produced by the platform's timer and not by the clause.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05058", "EV-GPS-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.free_wait.ends_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider does not contend that POL-NS-23's contact obligation was breached, and says so rather than stretching it. The chat log carries two in-app messages from the driver, at 07:40:00 (read by the rider at 07:40:22) and 07:46:20 (read at 07:46:30), and the trip record's in_app_calls carries two calls placed by the driver at 07:47:30 and 07:50:10 - all four before the 07:51:40 cancellation - with the derived contact_before_cancel block recording obligation_met as true. That route to voiding the fee is closed on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05058", "EV-TRIP-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.contact_before_cancel.obligation_met",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-24 is not engaged either, and the rider concedes it. The driver reached the pickup at 07:39:30, corroborated by the GPS trace within the 50 m STANDARD-zone arrival radius (nearest fix 1.758 m from the pickup at 07:40:40, accuracy 3.0 m), well before the scheduled time plus five minutes (07:50:00). The rider thus had no no-charge cancellation right on this trip, and the 5.00 SGD goodwill credit does not arise, because it additionally requires that the driver failed to attempt contact and the record shows two messages and two calls.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05058", "EV-GPS-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.driver_deadline.arrived_by_deadline",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on either party's profile can decide this trip. Only rider_profile.fraud_flags and driver_profile.fraud_flags (POL-GEN-22) and rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d (POL-NS-25) may be cited at all: both profiles carry no fraud flag, so no 0.95 confidence bar is raised, and the rider's 30-day no-show counter is not on the snapshot, so POL-NS-25's review flag does not fire. The rider's and the driver's rating, prior disputes, prior no-show flags and cancellation rates are context only under POL-GEN-01 and cannot be weighed against the rider on this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-05058", "EV-DPROF-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-NS-25", "POL-GEN-22"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's remaining submission is narrow and is put no higher than it is. The 5.00 SGD moved against the rider only through the platform's no-show automation, whose timer on this trip ran from the driver's early arrival and expired before the booked pickup time, contrary to POL-NS-21. The rider's own side of this record carries no trace at all: the GPS artifact's rider track is empty and rider_presence is unavailable, and the only third-party artifact, EV-ADVIS-05058-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0 and no payload. Where the ruling turns on a no-show finding produced by that automation, the rider asks the tribunal to keep the present state - the reversal already recorded and the 5.00 withheld from the driver - rather than convert it into driver compensation; and if the tribunal is not prepared to decide the no-show finding on this record, to hold the amount for a human reviewer under POL-GEN-26 rather than move it onto the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05058", "EV-GPS-05058", "EV-ADVIS-05058-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.available",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

