  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 5.0,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Driver, the 5.00 SGD no-show fee stands and is payable to you. Rider, the fee is not returned to you.\n\nWhat the record shows. The booking was for 07:45 (EV-TRIP-05058). The driver reached the pickup at 07:39:30 and the GPS trace (EV-GPS-05058) corroborates it: nearest fix 1.758 m from the pickup point at 07:40:40 with a reported accuracy of 3.0 m, inside the 25 m accuracy filter and the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius for this STANDARD zone, after which the fixes stay stationary at the kerb until 07:51:40. Because this was a scheduled trip and the driver arrived before the scheduled time, the 300 s free wait runs from the scheduled pickup (POL-NS-21; threshold free_wait_starts), i.e. 07:45:00 to 07:50:00 — exactly the trip record's derived free_wait block (starts_at 07:45:00, ends_at 07:50:00, free_wait_sec 300). The driver cancelled at 07:51:40, after the window (cancelled_after_free_wait = true). Before cancelling the driver sent two in-app messages (07:40:00, read 07:40:22; 07:46:20, read 07:46:30 — EV-CHAT-05058) and placed two in-app calls (07:47:30 and 07:50:10 — EV-TRIP-05058 in_app_calls), all before 07:51:40, so POL-NS-23's contact obligation is met and the fee is not voided. POL-NS-24 gives the rider no refund: the driver arrived at 07:39:30, well before the scheduled time plus five minutes (07:50:00), so there was no no-charge cancellation right, and no 5.00 SGD goodwill credit arises because that credit also requires that the driver failed to attempt contact, which he did not.\n\nThe rider's points. You are right that the platform's own wait timer started early, at 07:39:35, and expired at 07:44:35 — before your 07:45 booking — and that start is not the one POL-NS-21 authorises. But that does not decide the fee: the clause-correct deadline is 07:50:00 and the cancellation came at 07:51:40, after it, so the no-show finding holds on POL-NS-21 whatever the platform timer did. On your own account you came down at 07:53 — after both the 07:50:00 deadline and the 07:51:40 cancellation — and the trace carries no rider track putting you at the kerb earlier.\n\nFee and amount. The amount charged is 5.00 SGD (EV-FARE-05058: cancellation_fee 5.00, fee_matches_policy = true). POL-NS-22 therefore gives DRIVER_COMPENSATION with both amount fields equal to the 5.00 SGD fee, restoring to you what the interim reversal moved off you. No referral fires: the fee is exactly the policy fee of 5.00 SGD, so POL-NS-22's off-policy-amount referral does not apply, and POL-NS-25's repeat no-show flag does not apply because that rule operates only where rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d is present and it is not on this snapshot.\n\nEscalation is not engaged. The contested amount is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so under POL-NS-26 the AI ruling is final; neither profile carries a fraud flag, so the 0.95 confidence bar does not apply, and there is no safety indicator to trigger POL-GEN-21. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-05058-01, status MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0) carries no fact and no element of the no-show test depends on it, so it opens no question under POL-GEN-26.\n\nConfidence. Every artifact that carries a deciding fact — the trip record, the chat log and the GPS trace — is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so confidence is set at 0.90, above the 0.0 bar this value carries."
  },
