    "explanation": "This was a 07:45:00 scheduled pickup (TRP-05058, Block 108 Bishan Street 12). The 5.00 SGD no-show fee stands and is payable to the driver.\n\nTo the DRIVER: you arrived at 07:39:30, corroborated by the GPS trace (nearest fix 1.76 m from the pickup point with a reported accuracy of 3 m, inside the 25 m accuracy filter and the 50 m STANDARD-zone arrival radius), and you stayed at the kerb until cancellation. On POL-NS-21 the free wait for a scheduled trip on which you arrived before the scheduled time runs from the booked time, so it ran 07:45:00 to 07:50:00 (trip record derived free_wait: starts_from scheduled_at, ends_at 07:50:00, 300 s). You cancelled at 07:51:40, after it. You also met POL-NS-23 (v2.1 2.3): two in-app messages at 07:40:00 and 07:46:20 (both read) and two in-app calls at 07:47:30 (28 s) and 07:50:10 (20 s), all before cancelled_at. POL-NS-22 therefore applies: the fee of 5.00 SGD is charged to the rider and transferred to you, and the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with 5.00 SGD in both amount fields (amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd are the same figure, being the money the ruling moves). The interim reversal after the rider's complaint was expressly provisional and 'withheld from driver pending review'; it does not survive this review.\n\nTo the RIDER: you are right that the platform's own wait timer started on the early arrival (07:39:35) and expired at 07:44:35, and that POL-NS-21 does not authorise that start - the free wait runs from your booked 07:45:00. But that error does not change the result: read correctly, the free wait ended at 07:50:00, and the driver cancelled at 07:51:40, so the no-show conditions are satisfied on the clause itself. There is no refund route under POL-NS-24: the driver reached the pickup at 07:39:30, well before the 07:45:00 + 5 min deadline of 07:50:00, so no no-charge cancellation right arose, and the 5.00 SGD goodwill credit does not arise either because it also requires that the driver failed to attempt contact, whereas two messages and two calls were placed. Your own account puts you coming down at 07:53, after the window closed. The 5.00 SGD (fare ledger cancellation_fee 5.00, refund_issued_sgd 5.00, fee_matches_policy true, driver_compensation_if_upheld_sgd 5.00) is therefore restored to the driver.\n\nThe traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05058-01 is missing (status MISSING, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0); it carries no fact and nothing in the no-show test depends on it, so no open question arises under POL-GEN-26. No profile field decides this trip (POL-GEN-01), neither profile carries a fraud flag, there is no safety indicator (POL-GEN-21), and the contested amount of 5.00 SGD is below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so under POL-NS-26 the AI ruling is final. No condition producing a referral (POL-NS-22 fee-amount check, POL-NS-24 goodwill credit, POL-NS-25 repeat no-show flag - the rider profile carries no no_show_cancellations_30d field) is met.",
